# npm packages the web workspace may depend on directly (dependencies and devDependencies of
# every package.json under web/). Adding one is an owner action: propose it, with a reason and
# the decision or standard that chose it. `make check` fails if a package.json names a package
# not listed here. Format: <package name>  # <reason> (<D-ID or standard>)
react  # the web client's UI library (D193 §6; standards/typescript.md)
react-dom  # React's DOM renderer for the web client (D193 §6; standards/typescript.md)
typescript  # the language and `tsc -b`; held at 6.0 because typescript-eslint does not support 7 yet (D193 §6; standards/typescript.md)
vite  # build and dev server for both apps (D193 §6)
@vitejs/plugin-react  # React fast refresh and JSX transform for Vite (D193 §6)
vitest  # the test runner; shares Vite's transform (standards/typescript.md)
eslint  # the lint gate (standards/typescript.md)
@eslint/js  # ESLint's core recommended rules (standards/typescript.md)
typescript-eslint  # strictTypeChecked: no any, no assertions, no floating promises (standards/typescript.md)
eslint-plugin-react-hooks  # React's own rules of hooks and effects (standards/typescript.md)
@eslint-react/eslint-plugin  # missing keys, index keys, nested components, leaked listeners (standards/typescript.md)
eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y-x  # accessibility lint; maintained jsx-a11y fork that supports ESLint 10 (D188; standards/typescript.md)
@eslint-community/eslint-plugin-eslint-comments  # every lint suppression gives a reason (standards/typescript.md)
eslint-plugin-unicorn  # two rules only: no cryptic abbreviations, kebab-case filenames (standards/typescript.md)
globals  # browser and node global names for ESLint (standards/typescript.md)
prettier  # the formatter (standards/typescript.md)
dependency-cruiser  # module and package boundary rules (standards/typescript.md)
@types/react  # React's type definitions (D193 §6)
@types/react-dom  # React DOM's type definitions (D193 §6)
openapi-typescript  # generates the SDK's API types from api/openapi.json; a dev dependency (cut-a §5; web-client.md)
openapi-fetch  # the SDK's typed client over those types, the only code that calls the server (cut-a §5; web-client.md)
@noble/ed25519  # checks the core's Ed25519 signatures where the browser's WebCrypto has no Ed25519, as a Chromecast's Chrome 90 (the owner, 2026-11-12; idiosyncrasies.md)
i18next  # translation catalogues, from the first screen (D51; web-client.md)
react-i18next  # i18next's React binding; returnEmptyString false so an untranslated key shows English (D51)
hls.js  # HLS playback in every browser but Safari, which plays HLS natively (D217 §4; web-client.md)
jassub  # ASS subtitles drawn as their author styled them, over the video (D217 §4; web-client.md)
@playwright/test  # real browsers in tests: M3's playback timing in Chrome and Firefox, M4's two clients (D217 §4; D190)
qrcode-generator  # the registration link as a QR code, drawn in the browser; zero dependencies, MIT (D218 §1; the owner chose it, 2026-09-27)
happy-dom  # a DOM for vitest, so a test can render a screen, click it and read what it shows; a dev dependency (D190; the owner chose it, 2026-09-27)
@vitest/browser-playwright  # vitest's browser mode on the pinned Playwright: a test of what only a real engine does (layout, a stylesheet, WebRTC) in Chromium and Firefox with no server, in milliseconds where the browser tier takes seconds; a dev dependency (D190; the owner chose it after a trial, 2026-10-18)
